Here's the important nuance: **cutback weeks slow you down significantly**. Every 4th week, you're dropping mileage by about 20-25%, which means you're essentially "losing" a week of progression each cycle. Without cutback weeks, you'd hit 20-mile long run territory around week 7-8. But with those recovery weeks factored in, you're realistically looking at **week 11-12** for your peak 20-mile long run, with the taper kicking in around week 13.

This is actually a healthy timeline — it gives your body time to adapt to the increasing stress rather than just piling on miles. The cutback weeks aren't wasted time; they're when your body consolidates the fitness gains from the previous three weeks of building.

